-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- state programs through the factoring (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §12 “The build list”, “C. Memory and state”, item 23, C23: state programs through the fibers of a map)
-- a state of type A keyed by f : A → B is a point of the total space; a program that moves within
-- a fiber (a function on the fiber over each key) is a function on A through the equivalence,
-- and it leaves the key fixed: the projection after it is f. This is the shape of a world whose
-- state is keyed by what a map computes (a registry by its handle, an array by its index): an
-- update at a key is a program on that key's fiber, and the key's invariance is this theorem
in-fiber : {A B : Type} → (f : A → B) → ((b : B) → fiber f b → fiber f b) → A → A
in-fiber f g a = untotal f (f a , g (f a) (snd (total f a)))
